          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Noyb challenges LinkedIn's GDPR practice of selling profile visitor data back to users as a premium feature",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "European privacy advocacy group Noyb has filed a complaint arguing that LinkedIn violates GDPR Article 15 by processing users' profile visitor data and then charging them a premium subscription fee to access their own information. The complaint contends that under GDPR, individuals have a right to access data about themselves free of charge, making LinkedIn's monetisation model for this feature legally questionable. If upheld, the ruling could set a significant precedent affecting how any EU-regulated platform handles processed user data.",
            "url": "https://go.theregister.com/feed/www.theregister.com/2026/05/05/linkedin_gdpr_article_15_premium_noyb/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
